# IDE
.idea
.vscode
*.iml

# Backups. Each file here is a full database dump, so they must never enter a build
# context: they would bloat every build and bake the entire database into an image layer.
# `backups/` alone only matches the context root -- selfhost/backups is 0700 root-owned
# (that is what keeps the dumps unreadable), and the context sender fails outright on it
# with "permission denied" rather than skipping it. The ** form covers both.
backups/
**/backups
selfhost/backups

# Documentation
*.md
!README.md
LICENSE

# OS files
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# CI
.github/

# MCP config
.mcp.json
